for next AUTH value
On live server, set a strong real value for NEXTAUTH_SECRET in the environment file used by Docker runtime.
In your setup, keep it in .env and ensure .env.docker has the same value before deploy.


For production
cd /var/www/vendorpulse

NEW_SECRET="$(openssl rand -base64 48 | tr -d '\n')"

for f in .env .env.docker; do
  grep -v '^NEXTAUTH_SECRET=' "$f" > "$f.tmp"
  printf '\nNEXTAUTH_SECRET=%s\n' "$NEW_SECRET" >> "$f.tmp"
  mv "$f.tmp" "$f"
done

# verify exactly one key in each file (masked)
grep -c '^NEXTAUTH_SECRET=' .env .env.docker
grep '^NEXTAUTH_SECRET=' .env .env.docker | sed 's/=.*/=***masked***/'

For reload app/front runtime
cd /var/www/vendorpulse
